{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BorelPartialResolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BorelPartialResolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Infra.BorelRank"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BorelPartialResolution.borel_partial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BorelPartialResolution.borel_partial","kind":"theorem","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/BorelPartialResolution.lean#L14-L23","doc":"**Definitional unfolding of `borelRankPredicted`** (`prop:borel-partial-resolution`,\narithmetic core). `borelRankPredicted n r1 r2` evaluates to `r1 + r2` for even `n` and\n`r2` for odd `n` — a rewrite lemma exposing the definition, holding for every `n` (the\nearlier `2 ≤ n` hypothesis was unused decoration and is dropped). The *substantive*\nidentification with `K_{2n-1}^{ind}(F) ⊗ ℚ` is the (unproved) `BorelRank F` class, NOT\nthis equation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:borel-partial-resolution","label":"prop:borel-partial-resolution","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/borel-partial-resolution.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}